# Target C: close the four-weight-two-line perfect-matching subcase of the final k=4 p=3 profile

Date: 2026-09-26

Status: proof-level reduction plus exact finite support certificate. This closes only the
r=4 weight-two-line subcase of the remaining eight-no-root
k=4,D=-1,d_root=0,p=3 three-singleton profile. It does not close the
whole three-singleton profile, Target C-II, or Erdos Problem #99.

Companion verifier:

research/verify_target_c_support7_global_segment_relative_eight_noroot_k4_dminus1_d0p3_three_singleton_r4_perfect_matching_closure_2026_09_26.py

## 1. Inputs from current main

Current main gives a rank-four coefficient space P<=Q^8 with
(d1,d2,d3,d4)>=(2,4,5,7), and the mixed singleton-plus-pair profile is
closed, so p=3 consists of three singleton blocks.

In the present subcase there are exactly four projective weight-two lines.
Current main proves their supports are pairwise disjoint. Hence their supports
are four disjoint pairs M1,...,M4 partitioning the eight coordinates, and the
four lines form a basis of P. Thus P is the direct sum of four one-dimensional
pair-supported lines and its generalized Hamming weights are exactly
(2,4,6,8).

For every one of the three actual singleton blocks b, current main gives
dim((E_b+P)/P)=1 and proves that the quotient line is active on at least three
matched-pair quotient summands. Hence every singleton touch set meets at least
three matched pairs.

For every actual-empty touched block a, compatibility gives E_a<=P, and current
main proves that its generalized support, equal to its touch set, is a union of
whole matched pairs.

## 2. Touched-block bound

Let h be the number of touched root blocks, e the number of touched actual-empty
blocks, and c the number of touched complete blocks. All three singleton blocks
are touched, so h=e+3+c.

Because d_root=0, touched complete triangle rows are independent. The committed
face-local containment theorem gives rank H(T)-rank H(C)>=4. The triangle
boundary space on seven labels has rank at most 15, hence
c=rank H(C)<=rank H(T)-4<=11 and therefore e>=h-14.

Every actual-empty block has at least two incidences because its touch set is a
nonempty union of matched pairs. Every singleton has at least three incidences.
Every touched complete block has at least one. The eight no-root four-cycles
supply exactly 32 cycle-block incidences, so

32 >= 2e+9+c = h+e+6 >= 2h-8.

Therefore h<=20.

## 3. Necessary support conditions

Fix one support multiset and one perfect matching of its eight occurrence
coordinates.

A touched block is E-eligible only if its touch set is a union of whole matched
pairs. A rank-one empty block must have at least two touches; a rank-two empty
block must have at least four.

A selected singleton must meet at least three matched pairs. If its local empty
space has rank two, its singleton constraint is a nonzero line in P, so its
support contains at least one whole matched pair. Therefore the touch set of a
rank-two singleton must contain a whole matched pair as well.

These are only necessary conditions.

## 4. Virtual-state domination

The certificate searches a strict superset of actual states. For a fixed
matching, declare every E-eligible non-singleton touched block virtually empty,
even when it was complete in the actual state.

This relaxation preserves every actual state in the search: the virtual complete
set is a subset of the actual complete set, so independence is preserved and
rank H(T)-rank H(C) can only increase. Nominal coefficient-generation dimension
and generator support can only increase.

Let Eset be all E-eligible touched blocks and N=T\Eset. For a singleton triple
S, every block in N\S is forced complete in the virtual state. The verifier
requires:

1. all three selected blocks are singleton-eligible;
2. N\S is independent in the triangle-row space;
3. rank H(T)-|N\S|>=4;
4. the nominal coefficient dimension from virtual empty blocks plus the
   nonzero rank-two singleton constraints is at least four;
5. the available generator support covers all eight external coordinates, as
   required by d4(P)=8.

Phase data and exact gluing of the nominal local spaces into one P are omitted,
so the search is strictly larger than the actual-state search.

## 5. Exact finite certificate

The verifier enumerates all S7-orbits of multisets of eight tetrahedral
four-supports on seven labels, with support multiplicity at most three. It
reproduces the orbit counts

1,1,4,14,61,268,1283,6032,27763

for multiset sizes zero through eight.

Exactly 13,574 size-eight orbits satisfy h<=20. For every one of them the
verifier checks all 105 perfect matchings of the eight occurrence coordinates,
for 1,425,270 support-orbit/matching pairs.

Executed result:

support_multiset_orbits_size_8 27763
touch_at_most_20 13574
perfect_matchings 105
support_matching_pairs_tested 1425270
virtual_survivors 0

Therefore the r=4 perfect-matching subcase is empty.

## 6. Exactness of rank decisions

Support, matching, incidence, and canonicalization calculations are exact.

Triangle-row ranks are computed modulo 2^31-1. The verifier checks this Mersenne
prime by Lucas-Lehmer. Triangle rows have squared Euclidean norm three and the
rank is at most 15. The verifier checks (2^31-1)^2 > 3^15. Hadamard's
inequality therefore makes every modular triangle-row rank used here equal to
the rational rank.

## 7. Consequence

The remaining three-singleton profile has no r=4 branch. The weight-two-line
count is reduced to r=0,1,2,3. The next natural finite target is r=3, where
there is one unmatched coordinate pair and the sharp puncture conditions
strongly restrict the singleton quotient representatives.
